Saved-history replacement drafts for the demographic components of Figure S2; these do not reproduce the missing genetic PCA panel. Four pages retain all19 recovered audited summaries, including alternative input/grouping versions. Page1 contains candidate submitted-panel sources (pooled neutral core/peripheral and four archived genetic groups); their final production identity is not certified.
Lines show saved Ne medians; ribbons retain2.5th–97.5th percentiles from the archived Stairway summaries. No SFS model was refitted. Repeated constant curve vertices were compressed losslessly; all changing vertices and interval boundaries remain. Ne and time scales remain conditional on the SNP panel, folded SFS, projection, pooled structure and the stated but unverified callable sequence length L.
The archived scaling uses mu=2.538e-8 per generation and three years per generation. This is an assumed generation time times an annual synonymous substitution-rate proxy(8.46e-9), not a measured mutation rate for this species. Fixed-SFS rate sensitivity is available separately in the supporting audit. Absolute dates and sizes should not be presented as independently validated estimates.
Gray shading marks estimates younger than100assumed generations (300years); the dotted vertical line marks1000generations (3000years). These visual sensitivity horizons flag recent epochs rather than asserting a universal identifiability cutoff. All recent estimates and their uncertainty remain displayed. The time axis uses a pseudo-log transform (base10, sigma1year), linear near zero and approximately logarithmic at older times, to retain archived zero-year values without omission or arbitrary positive substitution.
The recovered individual popmaps assign101core,69peripheral,23adaptive_1 and24adaptive_2 individuals. The latter two groups include AC individuals as well as AZM/ZS and AYE/YL, respectively. Thus their names are archival genetic-group labels, not complete population identities or the published core/peripheral classification. nseq is the archived haploid SFS dimension and may be a projection; it is not asserted to be the number of sampled individuals.
Final source-version selection, caption wording, numbering, input provenance and recovery of the genetic PCA numerical results remain pending. All plots are evidence-review drafts.
